\section{Limitations}{

\strong{\code{stat = "identity"} requires a \code{violinwidth} column.} The default stat
(\code{"ydensity"}) computes \code{violinwidth} automatically. If you supply
\code{stat = "identity"} with pre-computed density data, your data frame must
include a \code{violinwidth} column (values in [0, 1] representing the
normalized half-width at each \code{y} level). If the column is absent,
\code{geom_violin_pattern()} emits a message and draws nothing for that group.
Note: \code{geom_violin()} itself also requires \code{violinwidth} and would silently
produce incorrect output in this scenario; \code{geom_violin_pattern()} makes
the requirement explicit.

\strong{\code{orientation = "y"} (horizontal violins) is not supported} for the
pattern overlay. The base violin renders correctly, but the pattern is
silently skipped. Use \code{coord_flip()} on a vertical violin as a workaround.

\strong{Pattern spacing is viewport-relative.} \code{pattern_spacing = 0.08} means
8\% of the violin's bounding box, so visual density is consistent across
violins of any width.
}

